WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.849
If you placed Mount Everest at the

00:00:02.899 --> 00:00:05.055
bottom of The Mariana Trench,

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:07.954
its snowy peak would still be buried

00:00:08.004 --> 00:00:10.690
under two kilometers of pitch-black ocean.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.205
Welcome to CurioSphere.

00:00:12.255 --> 00:00:15.469
Today, we descend into the hadal zone—a

00:00:15.519 --> 00:00:17.269
realm of crushing pressure,

00:00:17.319 --> 00:00:20.290
alien life, and mysteries science is only

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.805
beginning to decipher.

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:24.418
As you leave the sunlit surface,

00:00:24.468 --> 00:00:27.561
light disappears entirely within two hundred meters.

00:00:27.611 --> 00:00:30.460
Below that lies a world so hostile

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:33.358
that walking on the surface of the

00:00:33.408 --> 00:00:36.257
Moon is physically easier than visiting its

00:00:36.307 --> 00:00:37.307
floor.

00:00:37.357 --> 00:00:39.513
At eleven thousand meters down,

00:00:39.563 --> 00:00:42.412
the water pressure reaches over one thousand

00:00:42.462 --> 00:00:43.927
times atmospheric pressure.

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:46.825
Any standard submarine would be crushed like

00:00:46.875 --> 00:00:48.340
a soda can.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:51.361
Yet here, ghostly snailfish and translucent amphipods

00:00:51.411 --> 00:00:54.382
glide effortlessly, using unique organic molecules called

00:00:54.432 --> 00:00:57.280
piezolytes to prevent their cellular machinery from

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:58.330
collapsing.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:01.351
Near the seabed, hydrothermal chimneys spew mineral-rich

00:01:01.401 --> 00:01:04.493
water heated to four hundred degrees Celsius.

00:01:04.543 --> 00:01:06.293
In this sunlight-deprived darkness,

00:01:06.343 --> 00:01:09.436
life does not depend on the sun.

00:01:09.486 --> 00:01:11.643
Microbes consume toxic hydrogen sulfide,

00:01:11.693 --> 00:01:14.541
forming the base of an entirely independent

00:01:14.591 --> 00:01:15.649
food chain.

00:01:15.699 --> 00:01:18.548
We have mapped more of the surface

00:01:18.598 --> 00:01:21.446
of Mars than we have mapped of

00:01:21.496 --> 00:01:23.368
our own ocean trenches.

00:01:23.418 --> 00:01:26.267
Every expedition brings back species never before

00:01:26.317 --> 00:01:29.409
classified by science—reminding us of how little

00:01:29.459 --> 00:01:32.145
we know about our own world.

00:01:32.195 --> 00:01:35.044
The depths of our planet still harbor

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:37.779
ancient secrets waiting in the dark.

00:01:37.829 --> 00:01:40.678
What do you think is waiting to

00:01:40.728 --> 00:01:43.821
be discovered in the deepest ocean trenches?

00:01:43.871 --> 00:01:46.434
Share your theory in the comments,

00:01:46.484 --> 00:01:48.000
and subscribe to CurioSphere for more journeys
